Subject: [PATCH] partition: keep Next disabled while a background scan runs

The actions of the choice page revert the device and, for Erase, run the
autopartitioning in the callback of a background scan (ScanningDialog).
Next stays enabled meanwhile. Leaving the page before the callback ran
collects the partitioning jobs of an unchanged device, so the
installation creates no partitions and fails at the mount job. A person
hardly gets there in time, autoProceed does.

Run the scans through runScan(), which counts them, and report Next as
disabled while one is running.
